                <pb facs="0919" n="892" xml:id="pg892"/>

                <head>164. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Scowcroft) to President Bush<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d164-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1990-10-12">October 12,
                        1990</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>National Security Directive on START
                        and CFE</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Purpose</p>
                <p>To seek your approval of a proposed National Security Directive providing revised
                    U.S. positions on several START and CFE issues.</p>
                <pb facs="0920" n="893" xml:id="pg893"/>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Background</p>
                <p>I reviewed the major issues that remain in START and CFE with Jim Baker, Dick
                        Cheney, and Colin Powell
                    prior to Jim’s meetings with Shevardnadze
                    in New York. The proposed NSD at Tab A reflects the results of the New York
                    meetings and our agreement on how best to proceed on the remaining START issues in a way that will protect U.S.
                    national security interests while making every effort to complete both treaties
                    this year.</p>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">RECOMMENDATION</p>
                <p>That you sign the proposed National Security Directive at Tab A.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d164-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
